# DE-09 braking state-machine tunables.
#
# These live with the component rather than with one app so the logger's
# on-board preview and the transmitter's eventual DE-09 build are tuned from the
# same menu with the same symbol names.
#
# UNITS: Kconfig has no float type, so every threshold is an INTEGER here and is
# converted to float ONCE, at init, by the app glue that reads it
# (logger/software/main/fsm_preview.c). The suffix names the unit:
#
#   _MMPH      milli-mph          (1000 = 1.00 mph)
#   _MMPHPS    milli-mph/s        (2000 = 2.00 mph/s)
#   _MS        milliseconds       (no scaling)
#
# Defaults are the values the Python/JS reference was tuned to on real ride logs
# (BrakeTunables in tools/trc_viz.py). They are not arbitrary: changing one
# changes a calibrated safety behaviour, so retune against the captures in
# logger/ and re-run tools/fsm_check.py before trusting a new value.

menu "Braking state machine (DE-09)"

    config BRAKE_FSM_DECEL_ON_MMPHPS
        int "Rule 1 — decel trigger (milli-mph/s)"
        range 100 20000
        default 2000
        help
            OFF -> BRAKING fires when the derived deceleration exceeds this,
            held continuously for BRAKE_FSM_DECEL_ON_DEBOUNCE_MS.

            2000 = 2.00 mph/s. Lower turns the light on for gentler slowing
            (and on more throttle-off coasting); higher waits for harder
            braking.

    config BRAKE_FSM_DECEL_ON_DEBOUNCE_MS
        int "Rule 1 — decel-on debounce (ms)"
        range 0 2000
        default 120
        help
            How long the decel threshold must hold CONTINUOUSLY before the
            light turns on. Momentary throttle-off dips spike the wheel-speed
            derivative and clear within a tick or two; this rejects them
            without attenuating the signal (de-09 §4 explains why this is a
            debounce and deliberately not extra low-pass filtering).

            120 ms is the knee measured on the DE-07 40 mph ride log — larger
            values started clipping real short brake taps.

    config BRAKE_FSM_STOP_SPEED_MMPH
        int "Rules 2/3 — stop speed (milli-mph)"
        range 100 10000
        default 1000
        help
            Below this the bike counts as stopped: OFF -> STOPPED (rule 2) and
            BRAKING -> STOPPED (rule 3). Also the "rolling" qualifier on the
            launch guard (rule 6b).

            1000 = 1.00 mph.

    config BRAKE_FSM_MOVING_SPEED_MMPH
        int "Rule 6a — moving speed, STOPPED exit (milli-mph)"
        range 100 20000
        default 3000
        help
            STOPPED releases for motion only above this, giving low-speed
            hysteresis against the rule-2 entry threshold. This is what makes
            creep-in-traffic hold a steady light instead of strobing; on the
            DE-07 40 mph log the gap cut FSM transitions 162 -> 48.

            Must be greater than BRAKE_FSM_STOP_SPEED_MMPH. 3000 = 3.00 mph.

    config BRAKE_FSM_ACCEL_OFF_MMPHPS
        int "Rule 4 — accelerating-away threshold (milli-mph/s)"
        range 100 20000
        default 500
        help
            BRAKING -> OFF when acceleration exceeds this AND speed exceeds
            BRAKE_FSM_ACCEL_OFF_MIN_SPEED_MMPH. 500 = 0.50 mph/s.

    config BRAKE_FSM_ACCEL_OFF_MIN_SPEED_MMPH
        int "Rule 4 — minimum speed qualifier (milli-mph)"
        range 0 40000
        default 5000
        help
            Rule 4 is ignored below this speed, so a twitch of positive
            acceleration while nearly stopped cannot drop the light.
            5000 = 5.00 mph.

    config BRAKE_FSM_STEADY_BAND_MMPHPS
        int "Rule 5 — steady-cruise band (milli-mph/s)"
        range 100 20000
        default 750
        help
            While BRAKING, |accel| inside this band counts as steady speed;
            BRAKE_FSM_STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS of it releases the light.
            750 = 0.75 mph/s.

    config BRAKE_FSM_STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Rule 5 — steady-cruise timeout (ms)"
        range 100 20000
        default 1500
        help
            How long speed must stay inside the steady band before
            BRAKING -> OFF. Covers braking that trails off into a cruise
            without ever registering positive acceleration.

    config BRAKE_FSM_STOP_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Rule 6c — long-stop timeout (ms)"
        range 1000 600000
        default 60000
        help
            STOPPED -> OFF after this long at a standstill: parked, not
            waiting. The guard that covers a neutral stop, where the launch
            guard (6b) can never be true.

    config BRAKE_FSM_STATE_MIN_DWELL_MS
        int "Anti-strobe minimum dwell (ms)"
        range 0 2000
        default 250
        help
            Global floor on how soon after a transition the next one may
            happen. No single guard can strobe the light. DE-09 and
            docs/safety-regulatory.md both require this; flashing brake lights
            are illegal in many jurisdictions.

            This is a floor, not a substitute for hysteresis — see the rule-6a
            note in de-09-brake-decel-logic.md §4.

    config BRAKE_FSM_SPEED_SMOOTH_MS
        int "Wheel-speed low-pass before the slope (ms)"
        range 0 1000
        default 80
        help
            Time constant of the single-pole low-pass applied to wheel speed
            BEFORE the acceleration slope is taken. 0 disables it.

            Strictly this is a DE-08 decode-path value
            (can_decode_set_speed_smooth_ms), but it is calibrated together
            with the thresholds above and belongs to the same tuning set — it
            is `speed_smooth_ms` in the reference's BrakeTunables.

            It affects ONLY the derived acceleration. The decoded wheel-speed
            signal stays raw, so the DE-08 golden test is unaffected.

endmenu
